# Redesign v2

Direction: product-studio, dark base, one amber highlight. On this branch this file wins over design-standards.mdc where they disagree.

## Stack
- Next.js App Router (this repo is on 15, do not downgrade), TypeScript, Tailwind, React.
- Server components by default. "use client" only where interactivity needs it.
- No new dependencies unless a prompt approves them.

## Do not touch
- Game and live-product routes and their data: `/champions-draft`, `/rugby-draft`, `/pub-quiz`, `/games/longest-word`, `/draft`, `/wardrobe-ai`, `/stout-finder`. No edits to their pages, API routes, Supabase queries, Pusher code, or RLS policies. Linking to them is fine.
- Anything under `/hire` except where a prompt says so. The hire-meter finale, the Rudi easter egg, and the FELINE_DISTRACTION_DETECTED cat easter egg are intentional.
- Contact form handlers. All contact forms stay on Formspree.
- Secrets and Supabase keys. Never put them in client code.

## Routes
- Keep every existing route working. Change nav labels, not URLs.

## Copy
- No em dashes anywhere. Plain hyphens only.
- Banned words: passionate, journey, seamless, leverage, synergy, "crafting digital experiences", "I'd love to", "reaching out", "circling back".
- Plain, dry NI English.
- No invented testimonials, metrics, or client claims.
- Assisi rebrand: built, awaiting their sign-off. Never say they have adopted it.
- ShelterLink: ready for live use. Never say Assisi is using it.
- RV's Cold Brew: Square is linked, a few details left. Never claim working online ordering or payments.

## Design
- Tokens: base `#0A0A0F`, amber `#F59E0B`, DM Serif Display for display headings.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` everywhere.
